    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "见 after a verb: actually seeing or hearing",
      "body": "看 means 'to look' and 听 means 'to listen'. They describe the action, not whether it worked. Add 见 after them to show the result: you really saw or heard something. So 看见 is 'to see' and 听见 is 'to hear'.",
